^["risk_model"]{
 # hard: product name collides with an existing reg id → downstream selectors mis-hit
 # soft: `product` field absent from SpwPattern → BIAS preset falls back to withBoundaries:['body'] (broader match)
 # non_negotiable: `=`+body that carried NO product before must still parse and normalize identically except for the added product tag (no roundtrip regression)
}

^["validation"]{
 # hypotheses: [ "every current ={…} in the corpus normalizes unchanged except for product:'bias'" ]
 # negative_controls: [ "=[x] frame-only and bare = ops keep reg:'config' with no product", "'.'-facet product untouched" ]
 # demo_path: [ "spw:select a fixture --selector bias → hits the ={~\"...\"} node", "readBias(node) → { axis, targets, sign }" ]
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-22 19:10] decide — bias reading chosen over self-ref: self-ref is redundant with filename, collides with ~ (locative), and distributed self-declaration fights .spw/index.spw routing. bias is coherent with =:config and reuses register_bias arrays.
 >>[2026-07-22 19:12] observe — seam is normalize.ts:220; product is stamped only for '.'→facet today. `=`+body-only currently yields reg:'config' with an unnamed body coupling.
 >>[2026-07-22 19:14] observe — SpwPattern (query/types.ts) has no `product` field; BIAS preset can match `{sigil:'=', withBoundaries:['body']}` today but a precise product match needs the field + matcher support.
 >>[2026-07-22 19:15] observe — subject slot is gated to ^ and ? only (expressions.ts:278); `="reg"{…}` subject-binding is the one stretch form that touches the grammar.
 >>[2026-07-22 19:16] taste — target form composes cleanly: = says "lean toward", ~ says "this surface"; nesting keeps locative meaning with ~ and directional meaning with =, dissolving the self-ref tension.
 >>[2026-07-22 19:24] decide — all opens resolved by user: axis slot = frame [reg=depth] (match binding idiom); product id = `bias`; subject-binding IN scope (grammar touch at expressions.ts:278); mount consumption IN scope — spw:mount honors bias resolution, not just portable readBias.
 >>[2026-07-22 19:25] revise — commit sequence grows 6→8: add =-subject grammar commit and a cli-mount consumer commit. readBias stays the portable seam mount calls.
 >>[2026-07-22 19:31] decide — subject slot carries the ANCHOR (from-pole / biased entity), NOT the register name (register is already the frame [reg=…] — subject would be redundant). This makes `=` a binary relation anchor→targets; bare `={ }` = reflexive special case (anchor elided = enclosing node). Directly feeds mount: subject=key, body=target = a routing rule.
 >>[2026-07-22 19:32] taste — three slots earn three distinct jobs: subject=who, frame=along-which-register, body=toward-what. Keep subject monovalent (anchor only) — do NOT overload with scope guards (=(when:…){…}); that ambiguity is deferred to a separate concern.
 >>[2026-07-22 19:41] decide — WIDEN. Product is a neutral verb-polymorphic edge { anchor, axis, targets, sign }; meaning is chosen by the consumer verb, not baked into the product. Ship 3 consumers this branch: mount (resolution), mutate (rewrite; boon=apply/bane=revert; body-sequence = ordered patch), expand (template; unfold=boon, fold=bane — a specialization of mutate against a template edge).
 >>[2026-07-22 19:42] surprise — the rejected self-ref returns transformed: reflexive `={ ~"template" }` (anchor elided) is not location-declaration but PROVENANCE/lineage — "expanded from / conforms to this." The expand consumer reads exactly that.
 >>[2026-07-22 19:43] taste — invariant to protect: normalize/readBias must stay verb-neutral. No consumer word (resolve/rewrite/template) may leak into the seed product shape; seed emits the edge, CLI verbs interpret. This is the whole point of the polymorphism.
}

